      <h1>Follo.Money (Follo)</h1>
<h3>Follow the money</h3>
<p>Fund politics, and see how funding is used.</p>
<ol>
<li>Campaigns say how much they need, over time.</li>
<li>People donate to campaigns.</li>
<li>Everyone can see expenditures transparently.</li>
</ol>
<h3>How it works:</h3>
<ul>
<li>Anyone can create a campaign by giving it a name and a timed initial spending limit.</li>
<li>People donate to campaigns, knowing the campaign cant use more than what they’ve agreed to, for the specified amount of time.</li>
<li>Donors keep access to a portion of a campaign's surplus funds.</li>
<li>Keep in mind a campaign can change its spending after the initial limit’s duration, all surplus funds become accessible, the owner decides if and when to set another timed spending limit.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Why it works:</h3>
<ul>
<li>The public sector doesn’t benefit from private transactions. Winning politicians are doing things more transparently, more authentically.</li>
<li>People either prefer to be able to see where their money goes, or they're indifferent about it. No one strongly prefers their elected officials keep things from them.</li>
<li>The status quo is ActBlue (<a href="https://secure.actblue.com/donate/zohran-mamdani-transition-1/">https://secure.actblue.com/donate/zohran-mamdani-transition-1/</a>). It is a dead simple payment experience.</li>
<li>We've finally got the right tools to make this type of thing happen without relying on bankers.</li>
<li>The public sector should use efficient payment rails owned by the public sector.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Who's it for:</h3>
<p>Zohran. As Zohran continues asking for money, given his politics, he should prefer a system that allows him to be upfront about how much funds are needed, and his movement should prefer transparency and authenticity...</p>
<p>...so long as its also a dead simple experience for donors and campaign owners. The money has to flow.</p>

    
